### run 1
binCV -- goodFeaturesToTrack against OpenCV (the TIER 2 denominator)
OpenCV 4.10.0, cv::getNumThreads() = 1; binCV is single-threaded
frame 640x480, blockSize 3, maxCorners 200, qualityLevel 0.01, minDistance 33.33333
(the reference pipeline's parameters verbatim; word uint32_t)

 AGREEMENT with the OpenCV binarized pipeline over 4 frames:
 binCV corners 723, OpenCV corners 723, EXACT position matches 723
 worst displacement of a binCV corner from the nearest OpenCV one: 0.00 px
 (not bit-exact and not claimed to be -- TIER 2. The two sides share the
 covariance integers exactly; the remaining gap is the float eig map and
 how ties fall out of it.)

 YIELD against STOCK cv::goodFeaturesToTrack over 4 frames (the published denominator):
 binCV corners 723, stock corners 686 (1.05x), binCV corners within 3 px of a stock one: 540 of 723
 worst displacement 34.83 px -- DIFFERENT CORNERS, deliberately: stock runs a 3x3 Sobel
 over the byte image. This records comparable yield, not agreement.

 FRAME MAP vs STREAMING: 184 and 184 corners, 0 positions differ

